# travel
travel.module-desc=Prepares the environment, launches Baritone's elytra flight along a route with a decoy pattern, and restores everything on landing. Turning it on does not fly: the trip is launched with .xploits travel go.
travel.setting-destination-mode=COORDENADAS: a point in the world. RELATIVO: an offset in X and Z from where you are. AUTOPISTA: a distance along one of the eight axes, from where you are. Each mode has its own settings: switching modes does not reinterpret the previous mode's numbers.
travel.setting-x=Destination X coordinate. Meteor saves this value in meteor-client/modules.nbt: if you would rather the place you are going to not be written to disk, use RELATIVO mode.
travel.setting-z=Destination Z coordinate. It is saved to disk just like X: see that setting's warning.
travel.setting-offset-x=How far to move in X from where the trip starts. It is an offset, not a coordinate, and that also leaves less of a trail: Meteor saves its modules' settings in meteor-client/modules.nbt -when leaving the world and when closing the game, and every one that is not at its default value-, so a destination set in COORDENADAS ends up written to disk with its exact coordinates. An offset does not say from where.
travel.setting-offset-z=How far to move in Z from where the trip starts. It is an offset, not a coordinate, so what stays saved on disk is how far you move and not where you are going (see offset-x).
travel.setting-axis=The highway axis to travel along: the four cardinals and the four diagonals.
travel.setting-highway-distance=How many blocks to travel along the axis, counted from where the trip starts. They are FLOWN blocks, not blocks per coordinate: along a diagonal, 20 000 advance about 14 142 in X and as many in Z, and the flight measures 20 000. That way the number means the same on all eight axes.
travel.setting-highway-max-amplitude=The furthest the pattern may stray from the axis in highway mode (spec §4.2). With ESPIRAL it needs at least 338: a narrower spiral leaves the steps so close together that Baritone would land on almost all of them, and the module refuses to fly rather than let you believe you are turning.
travel.setting-waypoint-margin=How many blocks before an intermediate waypoint Baritone's goal is changed, so it has no time to land on it. The higher it is, the more it rounds off the pattern's corners.
travel.setting-pattern=The decoy pattern. SENUELO is rejected in highway mode, not downgraded (spec §4.2).
travel.setting-zigzag-amplitude=How far the ZIGZAG strays to each side of the heading, in blocks.
travel.setting-zigzag-period=Every how many blocks of progress the ZIGZAG switches sides.
travel.setting-quiebro-leg=Every how many blocks of progress the QUIEBRO breaks.
travel.setting-quiebro-offset=How far the QUIEBRO strays to each side of the heading, in blocks.
travel.setting-spiral-radius=How many blocks from the destination the final spiral starts.
travel.setting-spiral-turns=How many turns the spiral makes as it closes in on the destination.
travel.setting-decoy-angle=How many degrees the decoy strays from the real heading.
travel.setting-decoy-fraction=What fraction of the leg towards the decoy is flown before correcting.
travel.setting-baritone-prefix=The prefix Baritone reads its commands with. Only change it if you have changed it in Baritone.
travel.setting-auto-jump=elytraAutoJump during the flight: Baritone takes off on its own.
travel.setting-auto-jump-resting=The value elytraAutoJump is set back to on landing. It has to be declared: Baritone's settings can be written but not read (spec §6.1). Baritone ships it as false.
travel.setting-emergency-land=elytraAllowEmergencyLand during the flight: an emergency landing rather than a crash.
travel.setting-emergency-land-resting=The value elytraAllowEmergencyLand is set back to on landing. Baritone ships it as true.
travel.setting-conserve-fireworks=elytraConserveFireworks during the flight: use fewer fireworks in exchange for going slower.
travel.setting-conserve-fireworks-resting=The value elytraConserveFireworks is set back to on landing. Baritone ships it as false: set it to true only if you had it that way, because Baritone saves it to disk and all your manual #elytra flights would be slower from the first trip on.
travel.setting-firework-speed=elytraFireworkSpeed during the flight.
travel.setting-firework-speed-resting=The value elytraFireworkSpeed is set back to on landing. Baritone ships it as 1.2: set it to something else only if you had it that way, because Baritone saves it to disk and all your manual #elytra flights would keep that value from the first trip on.
travel.setting-nether-seed=The Nether seed, if known. Empty is left alone: without a seed Baritone turns terrain prediction off by itself, which is the right thing (spec §8.1).
travel.setting-notify=Local notice on launch, on passing a waypoint and on finishing. The loud warnings -the safety net, the stall and running out of fireworks- always show, whether you turn this off or not.
travel.setting-notify-sound=Sound on the loud warnings.
travel.setting-firework-warning=At this many fireworks or fewer the loud warning shows (spec §8). Zero only warns when you run out completely, which at 100 000 blocks is usually too late. Fireworks inside shulkers do not count.
